<title>USA: ContiFinancial unit prices $835 mln issue.</title>
<headline>ContiFinancial unit prices $835 mln issue.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>ContiMortgage Corp, a subsidiary of ContiFinancial Corp, said Thursday it has priced an $835 million Home Equity Loan Asset Backed Security issue. This issue is the second ContiMortgage securitization in 1997 and is structured using subordinated classes as credit enhancement, instead of a 100 percent surety wrap, as was the previous issue in January, said the company.</p>
<p>The bonds will be issued through ContiMortgage Home Equity Loan Trust 1997-2 and include 16 tranches as follows:</p>
<p>	Class	    Amount	Yield    Moody's/Fitch</p>
<p>		     ($ Thousands)</p>
<p>	A-1	   $  81,000	5.980%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-2	   $  65,800	6.295%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-3	   $ 113,400	6.543%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-4	   $  42,800	6.777%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-5	   $  39,200	7.000%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-6	   $  21,300	7.166%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-7	   $  35,500	7.405%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-8	   $  26,250	7.705%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-9	   $  39,375	7.150%    Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	A-10	  $ 251,100	 L+18     Aaa/AAA</p>
<p>	M-1F	  $  23,625	7.400%    Aa2/AA+</p>
<p>	M-2F	  $  30,187	7.628%	 A3/A</p>
<p>	B-1F	  $   6,563	7.936%   Baa3/BBB</p>
<p>	M-1A	  $  24,800	 L+34     Aa2/AA+</p>
<p>	M-2A	  $  19,375	 L+55	 A3/A+</p>
<p>	B-1A	  $  14,725	 L+85    Baa3/BBB</p>
<p>			 $835,000</p>
<p>The offering was lead by Credit Suisse First Boston. ContiFinancial is a finance company based in New York.</p>
